Comparison with the previous directional-C2 width-1e-12 control:

  quantity                    previous               masked PG2
  t=17/5 additive defect      about 3.6688e-09        3.6687611753e-09
  t=69/20 additive defect     about 1.12394e-06       1.1239343123e-06
  min4 additive defect        about 4.4320e-06        4.4318746579e-06

The improvement is negligible.  PG2 is much cheaper than propagating all 78
ambient Hessian pairs, but it does not remove the width-independent exchange
floor.  Its T and Q coefficients remain controlled; the incoming E object is
still a componentwise ambient box, and the close-encounter map amplifies that
already-lost correlation.  The next representation must carry a structured
remainder (for example a doubleton/tripleton arm or invariant-leaf chart), not
merely add more Taylor forms to a boxed E.
